@startuml
autonumber

' === Styling ===
skinparam sequence {
  GroupBorderColor black
  GroupFontColor black
  GroupFontSize 12
  BoxPadding 15
  LifeLineBorderColor black
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #f2f2f2
}

actor Bobby as User <<User>>
participant JPMDB as "JPMDB App" #e8e8e8
participant LAPI as "Sentry Login API" #d0e6ff
participant STS as "Sentry Token Service" #d0e6ff
participant FRS as "ForgeRock SaaS" #ffe5cc
participant SIDP as "IDA Identity Provider" #ffe5cc
participant EA as "Entitlement Adapter" #ffe5cc
participant DS as "Dispatcher Service" #d0e6ff
participant HIS as "Human Identity Service" #d0e6ff
participant KS as "Key Service" #d0e6ff
participant AS as "Authentication Service" #d0e6ff
participant EC as "Elastic Cache" #d0e6ff

== 0. Key Exchange & Setup ==
group Initial Key Setup
  AS -> KS: Request signing keys
  activate KS
  KS --> AS: Return signing keys
  deactivate KS

  STS -> KS: Request signing keys
  activate KS
  KS --> STS: Return signing keys
  deactivate KS

  STS -> EA: Request EA public keys
  activate EA
  EA --> STS: Return EA public keys
  deactivate EA

  JPMDB -> STS: Request Sentry public keys
  activate JPMDB
  STS --> JPMDB: Return Sentry public keys
  deactivate JPMDB

  EA -> STS: Request Sentry public keys
  activate EA
  STS --> EA: Return Sentry public keys
  deactivate EA

  note right of EA
  <b>EA stores Sentry public keys</b>\nfor JWT client assertion
  end note
end group

== 1. Primary OIDC Flow: JPMDB ↔ Sentry ==
group Primary OIDC Flow [JPMDB ↔ Sentry]
  note over User, LAPI
  <b>Primary OIDC Authorization Code Flow</b>
  end note

  User -> JPMDB: Access app
  activate JPMDB
  JPMDB -> JPMDB: Generate PKCE verifier & code_challenge
  JPMDB -> User: Redirect /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  deactivate JPMDB

  note right of User
  <b>Redirected to Sentry for OAuth2 login</b>
  end note

  User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  activate LAPI
  LAPI -> STS: Forward request
  activate STS
  STS -> FRS: Forward request
  activate FRS

  note right of FRS
  <b>FR checks if IDA auth is required</b>
  Uses custom_redirect_uri from config
  (client_id = agent name)
  end note

  FRS -> STS: Redirect /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  deactivate FRS
  STS -> LAPI: Redirect /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  deactivate STS
  LAPI -> User: Redirect /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  deactivate LAPI

  ' === NESTED OIDC FLOW ===
  == 2. Nested OIDC Flow: FR SaaS ↔ IDA ==
  group Nested OIDC Flow [FR SaaS ↔ IDA]
    note over FRS, SIDP
    <b>Nested OIDC Flow: FR SaaS ↔ IDA</b>
    <i>Embedded within Primary OIDC Flow</i>
    end note

    note right of User
    <b>User arrives at Sentry with IDA parameter</b>
    end note

    User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?idp=ida&client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
    activate LAPI
    LAPI -> FRS: Start federation journey
    deactivate LAPI
    activate FRS

    FRS -> FRS: Generate PKCE parameters for IDA flow
    FRS -> User: Redirect to IDA /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope&redirect_uri=[FRS_callback]
    note right of FRS
    <b>FR redirects user to IDA with</b>\nFR's callback URL as redirect_uri
    end note
    deactivate FRS

    note right of User
    <b>User redirected to IDA for authentication</b>
    end note

    User -> SIDP: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope&redirect_uri=[FRS_callback]
    activate SIDP
    SIDP -> User: Prompt for credentials
    User -> SIDP: POST /authenticate (User ID, Password)
    SIDP -> SIDP: Validate credentials
    SIDP <-> User: IDA session created
    SIDP -> SIDP: Validate client_id & redirect_uri
    SIDP -> User: Redirect to [FRS_callback]?code&state
    note right of User
    <b>IDA redirects back to FR callback URL</b>\nwith authorization code
    end note
    deactivate SIDP

    == 3. Federation Token Exchange & User Profile ==
    group Token Exchange via FR SaaS
      note right of User
      <b>User arrives at FR callback with code</b>
      end note

      User -> FRS: GET /callback?code&state
      activate FRS

      note right of FRS
      <b>FR exchanges code for tokens from IDA</b>
      end note

      FRS -> SIDP: POST /token (code, code_verifier, client_id, client_secret)
      activate SIDP
      SIDP -> SIDP: Verify PKCE & client credentials
      note right of SIDP
      <b>Code verifier matches challenge</b>
      <b>Client secret validated</b>
      end note
      SIDP --> FRS: Return access_token, id_token, refresh_token
      deactivate SIDP

      note right of FRS
      <b>FR normalizes user profile & updates shadow data</b>
      end note

      FRS -> DS: Update identity shadow
      activate DS
      DS -> HIS: Update identity shadow
      activate HIS
      HIS --> DS: Return identity data
      deactivate HIS
      DS --> FRS: Return identity data
      deactivate DS

      FRS -> FRS: Create Sentry session cookie
      FRS -> User: Redirect to Sentry /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
      note right of FRS
      <b>FR redirects user back to Sentry</b>\nto continue primary OIDC flow
      end note
      deactivate FRS
    end group
  end group

  note right of User
  <b>User returns to Sentry to continue</b>
  primary OIDC flow for Banking App
  end note

  == 4. Resume Primary OIDC Flow ==
  User -> LAPI: GET /authorize?client_id&code_challenge&state&scope
  activate LAPI
  LAPI -> STS: Forward request
  activate STS
  STS -> FRS: Forward request
  activate FRS

  note right of FRS
  <b>FR validates session and returns</b>
  authorization code for primary flow
  end note

  FRS -> STS: Return /authorize?code&state
  deactivate FRS

  STS -> EC: Store scopes for authorization code
  activate EC
  EC --> STS: Success
  deactivate EC

  STS -> LAPI: Return /authorize?code&state
  deactivate STS
  LAPI -> User: Redirect to JPMDB /authorize?code&state
  deactivate LAPI

  User -> JPMDB: Redirect with code&state
  activate JPMDB

  == 5. Token Exchange & Resource Access ==
  JPMDB -> LAPI: POST /token (code, code_verifier)
  activate LAPI
  LAPI -> STS: Forward /token (code, code_verifier)
  activate STS
  STS -> FRS: Forward /token request
  activate FRS
  FRS -> FRS: Validate session & PKCE
  FRS --> STS: Return access_token (aal=1)
  deactivate FRS

  STS -> EC: Request stored scopes for code
  activate EC
  EC --> STS: Return scopes
  deactivate EC

  STS -> EA: TokenExchange with scopes
  note over STS, EA
  <b>EA uses JWT client assertion</b>
  with Sentry keys for authentication
  end note
  activate EA
  EA -> EA: Validate Bobby's entitlement (simulate Sarah)
  EA -> EA: Switch sub=Bobby → Sarah
  EA -> EA: Sign token with EA private key
  EA --> STS: Return EA token (sub=Sarah)
  deactivate EA

  STS -> LAPI: Return access_token (aal=1)
  deactivate STS
  LAPI -> JPMDB: Return access_token
  deactivate LAPI

  JPMDB -> JPMDB: Verify token & show protected page
  JPMDB -> User: Present protected content
  deactivate JPMDB
end group

deactivate User
@enduml